From 71bc1ebb1c45e3eb8c20fe06f476179959ef02ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Hertenberger <erde74@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:35:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/25] ext4srv: say "file does not exist" as other file
 servers

A missing file gave "file not found". Plan 9's file servers and the
kernel say "file does not exist" (Enonexist), and programs look for it:
APE maps only that to ENOENT, so a POSIX program (gcc searching its -I
directories) took a missing file on ext4 for a hard error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/src/cmd/ext4srv/ext4.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sys/src/cmd/ext4srv/ext4.c b/sys/src/cmd/ext4srv/ext4.c
index aa017d1df..9cd937086 100644
--- a/sys/src/cmd/ext4srv/ext4.c
+++ b/sys/src/cmd/ext4srv/ext4.c
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ char Einval[] = "invalid operation";
 char Eio[] = "i/o error";
 char Enomem[] = "no memory";
 char Enospc[] = "no space";
-char Enotfound[] = "file not found";
+char Enotfound[] = "file does not exist";
 char Eperm[] = "permission denied";
 char Erdonlyfs[] = "read-only fs";
 
